<!--
    A pointer built through many nested choices must not stall the layout
    and guard walks.  The function is sub_d2f0 of angr-dev's MIPS ld.so.1
    (binaries/tests/mips/ld.so.1), its 9936 bytes copied at their link
    address.  Its STORE pointers pass a chain of MULTIEQUALs and additions;
    the stackstoreguard walk back along a pointer's definitions
    (kuna_storereach.rs pointer_pieces) visited every path, which never
    finished, and kuna decompile-all hung on the binary even with
    max-fn-seconds set.  The walk now remembers what each Varnode at each
    depth gave, so it visits each value once.  Stage: P3 heritage
    (stackstoreguard store windows) and P6 layout.  The assertion only
    asks that the function decompiles; before the fix this test never
    finished.
-->
